            <title>[LU-20998] lfsck OSP side memory leak fix and memory optimization. </title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20998</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;osp_it_fetch() allocates an array of 256 folios and 256 single page&lt;br/&gt;
folios for every OBD_IDX_READ, and osp_it_next_page() frees them as&lt;br/&gt;
soon as that bulk has been consumed, only for the next fetch of the&lt;br/&gt;
same iteration to allocate them again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The split leaks as well: the fetch assigns it-&amp;gt;ooi_folios&lt;br/&gt;
unconditionally, while the free is only reached once a bulk has been&lt;br/&gt;
consumed, which a failed fetch never is. As a failing&lt;br/&gt;
dt_index_operations::next is retried for as long as it fails unless&lt;br/&gt;
LPF_FAILOUT was asked for, every retry after such a fetch loses 1MB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the array for the life of the iterator and let osp_it_fini()&lt;br/&gt;
release it, which takes the allocation out of the fast path and&lt;br/&gt;
leaves no way to lose it. It is published once it is complete only,&lt;br/&gt;
so that a retry never reuses a half filled one. The old content of&lt;br/&gt;
a reused folio does not matter: only ooi_valid_npages of them are&lt;br/&gt;
read and every lu_page is validated by its magic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ask for the folios with GFP_NOFS, as the pages were asked for before&lt;br/&gt;
the switch to the folio API. These index objects are read with the&lt;br/&gt;
locks of the caller held, where a reclaim which re-enters this&lt;br/&gt;
filesystem can deadlock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fixes: 2b80459bf164 ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17916" title="Enable folio allocation support on the buffed io read/write path (BIO)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17916"&gt;LU-17916&lt;/a&gt; osp: switch to struct folio")&lt;/p&gt;</description>
